%C A236018 Does anyone understand what is colored (the entire array, the values, or the subblocks)? Are there sums of all nXk subarrays to be considered individually so we have nXk possible colors? Do the subblocks need to be contiguous (i.e. the 4 members of the subblock need to have row/column indices differing at most by 1)? How do different colors of all 3^((n+1)(k+1)) arrays effect the consideration of arrays as admitted or rejected in the number? The only obvious entry is the 81=3^(2*2) for the 2x2 array, where all arrays are admitted. - _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 04 2026
